# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/character
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/character> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/character> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CharacterPerformanceRole> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/character> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Character> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/character> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that links a character performance role to the character represented or performed in that role."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/character> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/character> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Character"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterPerformanceRole
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheatricalEvent> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CharacterPerformanceRole> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that is used to specify and link the details of characters in a creative work such as a play to the respective performers and the roles played by them."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Character Performance Role Property"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterRole
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheatricalProduction> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CharacterPerformanceRole> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that is used to specify the characters and the roles played by them in a theatrical play. For example, the role of 'Romeo' in 'Romeo and Juliet' by William Shakespeare is a character role."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Character Role"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterType
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Character> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that specifies the type of a character in a creative work or during an event. Examples of character types include person, animal, organization, puppet, robot, inanimate object, imaginary entity, etc."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/characterType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Character Type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/containsTheaterShowtimesRecord
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/containsTheaterShowtimesRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/containsTheaterShowtimesRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheaterShowtimesDataset> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/containsTheaterShowtimesRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource> .
<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/containsTheaterShowtimesRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that links a theater showtimes dataset to a theater showtimes record, for example a named graph or other RDF resource representing a record in the dataset."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/containsTheaterShowtimesRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/containsTheaterShowtimesRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Contains Theater Showtimes Record"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/creatorRole
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/creatorRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/creatorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheatricalProduction> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/creatorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/ProductionRole> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/creatorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that is used to specify the names of creator roles involved in a theatrical production that are, for instance, not characters in the play. For example, William Shakespeare performed the roles of playwright and creator in the production of his play 'Romeo and Juliet'."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/creatorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/creatorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Creator Role"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventRole
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Event> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/ProductionRole> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that is used to link the production roles in an event that features theatrical work such as a play to its performers. Event roles are (mostly off-stage) production roles that are performed during the preparation or performance of an Event. Examples include director, costume designer, stage manager, set/stage designer, lighting designer, sound designer, sound engineer, technical director, makeup artist, choreographer, understudy, usher, production manager, producer, funder, sponsor, front of house manager, etc."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Event Role Property"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventType
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Event> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that specifies theatrical event types such as Premiere, Last Performance, Guest Performance, etc."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/eventType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Event Type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/hasAccessibilityFeature
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/hasAccessibilityFeature> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/hasAccessibilityFeature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Place> .
