# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/accessibilityDescription
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/accessibilityDescription> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsDogs> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsServiceAnimals> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/AnimalPolicy> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://sozialhelden.github.io/a11yjson/describing-objects/0-model/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that describes if the place allows visitors to bring assistance/service dogs. Assistance dogs, also referred to as a service dogs, are a specific type of service animals that receive specialized training to aid an individual with a disability in navigating everyday life (source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assistance_dog)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allows Assistance/Service Dogs"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsDogs
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsDogs> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/AnimalPolicy> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsDogs> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://sozialhelden.github.io/a11yjson/describing-objects/0-model/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that describes if the place allows visitors to bring dogs in general."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allows Dogs"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsGuideDogs
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsGuideDogs> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsGuideDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsAssistanceDogs> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsGuideDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/AnimalPolicy> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsGuideDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsGuideDogs> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://sozialhelden.github.io/a11yjson/describing-objects/0-model/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsGuideDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that describes if the place allows visitors to bring guide dogs. Guide dogs are a specialized type of assistance dogs, trained to lead individuals who are blind or visually impaired around obstacles (source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guide_dog)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsGuideDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsGuideDogs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allows Guide Dogs"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsServiceAnimals
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsServiceAnimals> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsServiceAnimals> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/AnimalPolicy> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsServiceAnimals> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsServiceAnimals> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://sozialhelden.github.io/a11yjson/describing-objects/0-model/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsServiceAnimals> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A property that describes if the place allows visitors to bring service animals along. A Service Animal is an animal that has been trained to assist a disabled person (source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Service_animal). While dogs are the most common service animals, other animals (like miniature horses, ferrets, parrots, and monkeys) may also serve in this role, depending upon regional regulations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsServiceAnimals> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/allowsServiceAnimals> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allows Service Animals"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/hasSpaceForAssistant
