<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/AnimalPolicy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class that describes the policies of a place concerning bringing animals along."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/AnimalPolicy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/AnimalPolicy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Animal Policy Class"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Character
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Character> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Character> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class that represents a character in a creative work such as a Play.\n    Examples of characters include:\n    Romeo (from Romeo and Juliet by William Shakespeare; character type: Person),\n    Alexander Hamilton (from Hamilton musical by Lin-Manuel Miranda; character type: Person),\n    Simba (from The Lion King; character type: Animal),\n    Kermit the Frog (from The Muppet Show; character type: Puppet),\n    WALL-E (from Pixar's WALL-E movie; character type: Robot),\n    Puck (from A Midsummer Night's Dream by William Shakespeare; character type: Imaginary Entity/Fairy),\n    the flying Magic Carpet (from Aladdin; character type: Inanimate Object), etc."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Character> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Character> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Character"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CharacterPerformanceRole
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CharacterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CharacterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Role> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CharacterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class that links a character role to its performer.\n    Characters can be from a creative work such as a Play.\n    Examples of characters include Romeo (from Romeo and Juliet by William Shakespeare; characterType: Person), Alexander Hamilton (from Hamilton musical by Lin-Manuel Miranda; characterType: Person), Simba (from The Lion King; characterType: Animal), Kermit the Frog (from The Muppet Show; characterType: Puppet), WALL-E (from Pixar's WALL-E movie; characterType: Robot), Puck (from A Midsummer Night's Dream by William Shakespeare; characterType: Imaginary Entity (Fairy)), the flying Magic Carpet (from Aladdin; characterType: Inanimate Object), etc.\n    Performers can include persons, animals, organizations, puppets, robots, inanimate objects, or even computer-generated imagery (CGI) in a creative work or during an event."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CharacterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CharacterPerformanceRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Character Performance Role Class"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CulturalOrganization
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CulturalOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CulturalOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Organization> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CulturalOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class for organizations in the culture domain, such as theaters, museums, libraries, orchestras, and cultural associations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CulturalOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CulturalOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cultural Organization"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/DataService
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/DataService> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/DataService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#DataService> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/DataService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://schema.org/Service> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/DataService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class for data services that provide access to datasets or records."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/DataService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/DataService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Data Service"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Event
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Event> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://schema.org/Event> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class that describes a thing happening at a particular location and at a particular time such as a theatrical play performance, movie screening, concert, or festival."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Event> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Event"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Organization
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Organization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class for describing organizations. It extends schema:Organization and can be associated with data services and other organizational metadata."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Organization"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Performer
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Performer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Performer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class that specifies the performer of a role in a creative work or event. Performers can include persons, animals, organizations, puppets, robots, inanimate objects, or even computer-generated imagery (CGI)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Performer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Performer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Performer"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PerformingArtsTheater
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PerformingArtsTheater> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PerformingArtsTheater> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://schema.org/PerformingArtsTheater> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PerformingArtsTheater> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Place> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PerformingArtsTheater> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A place such as a building, a group of buildings, or an event site that is designated for organizing theatrical events such as plays."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PerformingArtsTheater> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PerformingArtsTheater> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Performing Arts Theater"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Place
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Place> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://schema.org/Place> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class that describes a physical place or location. The drk:Place class extends schema:Place to describe the accessibility features available at the place."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Place> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Place"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PlaceAccessibilityFeature
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PlaceAccessibilityFeature> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PlaceAccessibilityFeature> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://sozialhelden.github.io/a11yjson/describing-objects/0-model/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PlaceAccessibilityFeature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class that describes the physical (and sometimes human-rated) accessibility of a physical place."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PlaceAccessibilityFeature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/PlaceAccessibilityFeature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Place Accessibility Feature Class"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/ProductionRole
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/ProductionRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/ProductionRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Role> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/ProductionRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class that links a production role to its performer.\n    Production roles can, in general, include creator roles, non-character roles, offstage or behind-the-scenes roles.\n    Examples of production roles include creator, writer, playwright, costume designer, stage designer, choreographer, makeup artist, understudy, usher, funder, sponsor, etc."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/ProductionRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/ProductionRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Production Role"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Role
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Role> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://schema.org/Role> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class that links a role to its performer.\n    Roles can, in general, be of various types such as character roles, production roles, event roles, onstage roles, offstage or behind-the-scenes roles.\n    Examples of role names include creator, writer, playwright, actor, protagonist, puppeteer, singer, cameo, costume designer, stage designer, choreographer, makeup artist, understudy, funder, sponsor, etc.\n    Performers can include persons, animals, organizations, puppets, robots, inanimate objects, or even computer-generated imagery (CGI) in a creative work or during an event."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/Role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Role"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheaterOrganization
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheaterOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheaterOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://schema.org/TheaterGroup> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheaterOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/CulturalOrganization> .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheaterOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class for theater organizations, such as theater groups, companies, or associations, that provide information about theatrical productions and events."@en .
<https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/TheaterOrganization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/drk/ontology/> .
