# http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A company or organization performing a role in the production of a creative work, e.g., by funding or sponsoring it."@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Organization Performer"@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organization> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://dbpedia.org/ontology/Organization> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q43229> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#> .
# 
# http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A human individual that performs a role in the production or performance of a creative work such as a play or a movie. For example, William Shakespeare performed the role of author in the production of his play 'Romeo and Juliet'; Christian Bale performed the roles of 'Actor' and 'Protagonist' while playing the characters of 'Batman' and 'Bruce Wayne' in Christopher Nolan's 2008 movie 'The Dark Knight'."@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Person Performer"@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Person> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Human Performer"@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://dbpedia.org/ontology/Person> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://schema.org/Person> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Person> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#> .
# 
# http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppet
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppet> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppet> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppet> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An inanimate figure or model manipulated by a puppeteer that performs a role in a creative work such as a play or a movie. For example, the kermit puppet artifact that featured as 'Kermit the Frog' in 'The Muppet Show'. Jim Henson's original Kermit is currently on display at the National Museum of American History."@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppet> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Puppet Performer"@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppet> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puppet> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppet> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1913135> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppet> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#> .
# 
# http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A person who manipulates a puppet in the performance of a creative work such as a play or a movie. For example, Jim Henson as the puppeteer for 'Kermit the Frog' in 'The Muppet Movie' (1979)."@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Puppeteer Performer"@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puppeteer> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://dbpedia.org/ontology/Person> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://schema.org/Person> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Puppeteer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2629392> .
