# http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Robot
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Robot> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Robot> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Robot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A machine, especially one that can be programmed, that performs a role involving complex physical activities in a creative work such as a play or a movie. For example, 'Robby the Robot' from the 1956 film Forbidden Planet, which has been showcased at the Smithsonian National Museum of American History; 'T-800' from the Terminator film series, etc."@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Robot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Robot Performer"@en .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Robot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robot> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Robot> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11012> .
<http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#Robot> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://w3id.org/drk/vocabs/performer-types#> .
